  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "According to the article, the flight has been termed \"The Impossible Landing\", as it is considered one of the most impressive landings in the history of aviation.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383099056:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:09Z",
      "text": "United Airlines Flight 232 was a regularly scheduled flight from Stapleton International Airport in Denver to O'Hare International Airport in Chicago, continuing to Philadelphia.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383099056:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:18Z",
      "text": "The flight set out from Stapleton International Airport, bound for Philadelphia International Airport.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383099056:origin",
        "wiki:box:1383099056:destination"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "It came down about 770 km from Stapleton International Airport in a straight line, with about 1,790 km still to go.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383099056:origin",
        "wiki:box:1383099056:destination",
        "wiki:box:1383099056:coordinates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "At Sioux Gateway Airport, an uncontained engine failure caused by fan disk separation led to a loss of hydraulics and a loss of control.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383099056:summary",
        "wiki:box:1383099056:coordinates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:42Z",
      "text": "The aircraft was a McDonnell Douglas DC-10-10, operated by United Airlines, a type built by McDonnell Douglas that first flew in 1970.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383099056:aircraft",
        "wd:Q208075:P176",
        "wd:Q208075:P606",
        "wiki:box:1383099056:operator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:51Z",
      "text": "According to the article, 112 of the 296 people on board died and 184 survived.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383099056:occupants",
        "wiki:box:1383099056:fatalities",
        "wiki:box:1383099056:survivors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:02Z",
      "text": "Flight 232 departed Stapleton International Airport in Denver at 14:09 Central Daylight Time, en route to O'Hare in Chicago, with continuing service to Philadelphia.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:timeline:1383099056:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:09Z",
      "text": "At 15:16, while the airplane was making a slight right turn at its cruising altitude of 37,000 ft, the fan disk of its tail-mounted General Electric CF6 engine disintegrated explosively.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:timeline:1383099056:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:16Z",
      "text": "Senior flight attendant Jan Brown Lohr relayed the message to the flight crew, who invited Fitch into the cockpit, and he began assisting at about 15:29.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:timeline:1383099056:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:24Z",
      "text": "The rear engine's fan disk and blade assembly, about 8 ft across, could not be located at the accident scene despite an extensive search.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383099056:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:31Z",
      "text": "The engine's manufacturer, General Electric, offered rewards of $50,000 for the disk and $1,000 for each fan blade.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383099056:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:38Z",
      "text": "Three months after the crash, a farmer found most of the fan disk, with several blades still attached, in her cornfield, and a General Electric lawyer confirmed this qualified her for a reward.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:investigation:1383099056:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:46Z",
      "text": "English Wikipedia recorded 51,857 readers of the article on 2 November 2026, about 39× the usual.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:United_Airlines_Flight_232:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:United_Airlines_Flight_232:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:53Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 11 languages, and after English, Japanese had the most readers, at 167.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:United_Airlines_Flight_232:2026-11-02",
        "views:ja:ユナイテッド航空232便不時着事故:2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:02:00Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers; a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:ja:ユナイテッド航空232便不時着事故:2026-11-02",
        "views:de:United-Airlines-Flug_232:2026-11-02",
        "views:zh:聯合航空232號班機空難:2026-11-02",
        "views:es:Vuelo_232_de_United_Airlines:2026-11-02",
        "views:fr:Vol_United_Airlines_232:2026-11-02",
        "views:ru:Катастрофа_DC-10_в_Су-Сити:2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:02:10Z",
      "text": "The sources are Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata, and each caption links to the evidence it rests on.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383099056:6",
        "views:en:United_Airlines_Flight_232:2026-11-02",
